// =====================================================================================
// D4 - Workload identity accessed a resource for the first time
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Maps to  : POC Test C - Anomalous Fabric Access by a Workload Identity
// Table    : AADServicePrincipalSignInLogs  (diagnostic category: ServicePrincipalSignInLogs)
// Severity : 3 (Informational)
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// What it finds
//   A service principal requesting a token for a resource it has never successfully
//   touched in the preceding 14 days. This is a home-grown approximation of what Entra's
//   anomalousServicePrincipalActivity detection does natively once it has a baseline.
//
// Why it matters
//   POC Test C is the concrete case: an identity provisioned to read Azure SQL suddenly
//   asks for a Power BI / Fabric token. Nothing is technically wrong - the permission
//   may even be granted - but the pivot itself is the signal. An attacker exploring what
//   data a stolen credential can reach looks exactly like this.
//
// Important caveats
//   - This is deliberately severity 3. It is a lead, not a verdict.
//   - It is NOISY for the first 14 days after deployment because the baseline is empty.
//     Expect that, and do not tune it down before the window fills.
//   - New legitimate integrations will fire it. That is working as intended: a workload
//     identity reaching a new resource should be a known, ticketed event.
//
// Triage
//   1. Is there a change record for a new integration on that identity?
//   2. Does the new resource fit the identity's stated purpose?
//   3. Correlate with D3 - a first-time access that is part of a burst is far worse than
//      a single first-time access.
// =====================================================================================

let BaselineWindow = 14d;
let DetectionWindow = 1h;
let KnownPairs =
    AADServicePrincipalSignInLogs
    | where TimeGenerated between (ago(BaselineWindow) .. ago(DetectionWindow))
    | where ResultType == 0
    | distinct ServicePrincipalId, ResourceDisplayName;
AADServicePrincipalSignInLogs
| where TimeGenerated > ago(DetectionWindow)
| where ResultType == 0
| join kind=leftanti KnownPairs on ServicePrincipalId, ResourceDisplayName
| summarize
    FirstAccess = min(TimeGenerated),
    SignIns     = count(),
    SourceIPs   = make_set(IPAddress, 10)
    by ServicePrincipalName, ServicePrincipalId, AppId, ResourceDisplayName
| order by FirstAccess desc
